## Cycle-style delivery

Features ship as numbered cycles with a written plan in `docs/plans/` before any code. Plans live ~30–60 tasks each. Never start a cycle without one.

**Cycle done = all of**: zero pending tasks in plan, integration suite green (0 failed), full test suite green, `migrate-smoke` green if migrations changed, pre-commit clean, manual smoke of the user-visible feature, branch merged to the project's merge target (`.harness/branches.yaml`, default `{{BASE_BRANCH}}`).

Use `scripts/harness/cycle_done.py --plan <file>` to close a cycle. Use `scripts/harness/validate_plan.py <file>` to validate a plan before starting it.

## Parallel work (worktrees)

To start a change in its own working directory (parallel branches without the
stash-dance), invoke `/leash-start-work`. It creates `.worktrees/<slug>` on a
`<type>/<slug>` branch off `{{BASE_BRANCH}}` — the physical form of "branch first, edit
after". Opt-in; it never weakens branch discipline. Remove the worktree after
merge with `git worktree remove .worktrees/<slug>`.

## Worktree leash (main is read-only)

The harness installs a **worktree leash**: a `PreToolUse` gate denies any
`Edit`/`Write`/`MultiEdit`/`NotebookEdit` whose target is in the **main
worktree**. All edits target files in a linked worktree — run
`/leash-start-work` to create one (`.worktrees/<slug>` on `<type>/<slug>`
from `{{BASE_BRANCH}}`), then edit the files there. This makes concurrent sessions safe
by construction: each works in its own worktree, nobody edits the shared
main tree. Clean up with `/leash-finish-work`.

The session itself **stays rooted in the main checkout** — never start or
move a Claude Code session inside `.worktrees/<slug>` (session history is
keyed to the session root and is lost when the worktree is removed). The
`session_root_guard` SessionStart hook warns if a session is rooted in a
linked worktree.

For a one-off direct edit to the main tree, authorize a single write:
`python -m scripts.harness.allow_main_write "<reason>"` (logged to
`.harness/exceptions.log`), then retry the edit.

Repos with `workflow: branch` in `.harness/branches.yaml` use disciplined
checkouts instead of worktrees: `/leash-start-work` runs `git checkout -b
<type>/<slug>` in place rather than creating a linked worktree, and edits
are allowed only while HEAD is on a `<type>/<slug>` branch — everything
else is denied by the same gate.
